                <pb facs="0312" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg198"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/5252: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Shoemaker</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-31T12:00:00+02:00">October 31,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received October 31—10:25 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>28. Department’s telegram No. 9, October 30, 1 p.m.<anchor n="95"
                        xml:id="d145-f1"/> Formula calculated to avoid establishing principle of
                    “compensation” but obligating Bulgaria during current moratorium year to
                    continue reparation payments in favor of Greece equal to Kafandaris-Molloff
                    payments by latter presented at Athens by the Bulgarian Government October 24th.
                    Since then Bulgarian Foreign Office has been expecting Greek response daily. As
                    soon as this is received I shall inform the Department of its nature by
                    telegraph.</p>
                <p>Official opinion here is that response must be in the affirmative if Greece is
                    acting in good faith as formula fully satisfies demands made by Greece before
                    London Committee of Experts.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Shoemaker</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
